# Tor client configuration for the tor-proxy container
#
# Bind SOCKS5 to all interfaces so the published 9050 port works from
# other machines on the network. (Tor default binds to 127.0.0.1 only,
# which would make a published port unreachable from outside.)
# Tor logs a "non-loopback address" notice at startup - expected here:
# this container is an intentional LAN proxy service.
SocksPort 0.0.0.0:9050

# Write notices directly to the log file (no stdout/tee pipeline needed)
Log notice file /var/log/tor/notices.log
